From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:00:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] softisp: complete failed GPU frames

Complete failed EGL debayer frames instead of leaving their input and
output buffers queued indefinitely. Preserve the captured sequence and
timestamp, mark the output FrameError and clear its used length.

Emit invalid statistics for failed frames so the IPA still produces the
metadata required by the simple pipeline to complete each request.
Explicitly invalidate failed statistics even on scheduled statistics
frames; never reuse an earlier frame's samples as valid. Route a failed
CPU mapping for statistics through the same error path.

Release CPU DMA access and wait for any submitted GPU work before
returning either buffer. A draw can report an error after other GPU
accesses have already been queued. Leave the successful rendering,
statistics cadence and optical parameters unchanged.

Add a sensor-free EGL regression test with real DMA buffers for input
mapping failure, output import failure and a GL error after draw
submission, including recovery on subsequent successful frames and
stale-statistics rejection. Register it with Meson when GPU SoftISP is
enabled and as the Android libcamera_debayer_egl_test target.

Base-commit: df8e348d64b4932a0676256ed24f0da3ee9438bc
---
